      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I've already started looking at the dates, and it doesn't look like it's tied to a specific person or department. It's just these little oddities appearing out of nowhere in the ledger. Besides just matching receipts, are there any specific statistical methods or data analysis techniques I could use to distinguish between random, human error (like a typo) and something more intentional or organized? I want to be sure I'm not chasing ghosts.",
