      "content": "You can utilize descriptive statistics to analyze the frequency and magnitude of these discrepancies; if the amounts consistently cluster around a specific range or follow a pattern that deviates from normal distribution, it may suggest a systemic issue rather than random noise. Additionally, applying a control chart can visualize this data over time, helping you distinguish between stable random variation and potential shifts caused by intentional manipulation. If the variance exceeds acceptable statistical limits despite no human latency, investigating the IT configuration or manual entry software for hidden default settings would be your next logical step.",
