      "role": "user",
      "content": "The control chart idea is helpful, I'll try setting that up in Excel. One thing that's bothering me is how \"unseen\" these are. They aren't large enough to trigger any automated flags, but they're just enough to be a nuisance and mess with the reconciliation. It almost feels like someone is intentionally trying to stay under the radar with these small, persistent little blips. Is there a way to look for \"stealthy\" patterns where the discrepancies are specifically sized to avoid detection thresholds?",
